<speak>That is a very recognisable distinction. An item can be noticed without being dealt with, and a visible place for unfinished administration can help. We can also keep our routine messages concise, with the administrative purpose near the beginning rather than buried under a long introduction. If there is something that needs a separate conversation, it is better to make that clear in the scheduling note. For general correspondence preferences, would you rather have digital material as your usual reference point, with paper retained only where appropriate, or do you still find it easier to work mainly from physical documents at home?</speak>